  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Food-Court Coupon Booklet",
    "overview": "Every amount owed is a numbered coupon torn from the trip's own booklet. The world is the coupon stock of a Thai food court: white paper slips on a cool pale ground, a deep ink green-black for the shell and all text, one pastel coupon tint per member, and small red serial numbers printed in a corner. Perforations are dashed lines, and a payment that is confirmed tears off along its perforation.\n\nThe density is phone-first and single column, at most 512px wide, built for one hand and mixed-age eyes. Rank comes from weight before size: a four-step type scale, with section headings at body size in bold rather than in a larger size. State is carried by line form instead of colour: dashed means pending, solid means settled, struck through means the money did not move.\n\nThe world rejects the fintech dashboard (white cards, a green accent, charts) and the green/red money ledger. Balances are ink amounts with words (\"คุณต้องโอนรวม\", \"เพื่อนต้องโอนให้คุณรวม\"), never a sign colour.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Ink green-black shell and text on a cool pale ground; white coupons on top.",
      "One coupon tint per member, by join order, reused for their tile, their payer chip and coupons they are owed.",
      "Red only for serial numbers (and, through the owe tokens, error and destructive text).",
      "Amounts and serials in Kanit with tabular figures; every other word in Anuphan.",
      "Dashed perforations as both decoration and state.",
      "Small coupon corners (10px); no pills."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Serial Red Rule",
        "body": "Red is for serial numbers. Errors and destructive actions use the owe tokens. No other surface, icon or amount is red.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Ledger Rule",
        "body": "Balances are ink amounts with words that say which way the money goes. Never use green for money in and red for money out.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Tint Per Member Rule",
        "body": "A member keeps the same tint everywhere for the whole trip, assigned by join order. Tints mark people, not states.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Four Steps Rule",
        "body": "The scale has four steps: meta 14, body 16, title 22, display 34. Rank comes from weight first, then size. Nothing readable is below 14px; the 13px serial is the only exception, and it is a mark, not a sentence.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Coupon Numerals Rule",
        "body": "Every amount, serial and count is set in Kanit with tabular figures. Words are never set in Kanit.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Paper Rule",
        "body": "Coupons and cards lie flat. The only cast shadow belongs to the one control that floats over content.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Line Form Rule",
        "body": "Dashed means pending or not settled, solid means settled, struck through means cancelled or rejected. Pending chips, pending notices and claims awaiting confirmation always carry a dashed edge.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do give every coupon a serial number in serial red, 13px Kanit semibold.",
      "Do show which way money goes with words and an ink amount, never with a sign colour.",
      "Do keep each member on one tint for the whole trip, assigned by join order.",
      "Do use dashed edges for pending, solid for settled, and strikethrough for cancelled.",
      "Do keep to the four type steps (14, 16, 22, 34) and build rank with weight first.",
      "Do keep touch targets at least 44px tall (48px for primary actions).",
      "Do keep PromptPay's own navy (#1b3f73) on the QR panel."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use red for anything except serial numbers; errors and destructive actions use the owe tokens.",
      "Don't colour balances green and red like a bank ledger.",
      "Don't set readable text below 14px.",
      "Don't use pill-shaped buttons, chips or badges.",
      "Don't add drop shadows to coupons or cards.",
      "Don't build a fintech dashboard of white cards, a green accent and charts."
    ]
  }
}